 You should make an incision and suck out the venom;

Try it yourself, but I just don't think it would be as practical as it might be if it was a rattlesnake bite. Why? Because when you're bitten by one of these snakes, the venom is usually injected into the vein. Sometimes, the venom will also be injected into the muscle. As a result, you need to have a lot of good healthy blood on hand. After all, when the venom enters your body, your blood will carry it through your system.

